# L §4.6 step 1: "a key it leaves unstated, or covers with *, is one its index or kind had on the row's known date.
# A default row stated before a key was added doesn't cover that key (§6.2)."  ks gains c in a version known
# 2026-06-01; the default row x[*] = 1 is known 2026-01-01: x[c] is a hole (no value at the law date), x[a] is 1.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ks = [a, b]
input x[k in ks]: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x[*] = 1

version v2
  cite s
  known 2026-06-01
  ks + [c]

ask q1: x[a], x[c] law 2026-07-01
=== expect
q1: (1, ?"x at c: no value at 2026-07-01" (x[c]))
  law date 2026-07-01, cut 2026-12-31
